#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:6
msgid "Hexagon System emulator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:8
msgid ""
"Use the ``qemu-system-hexagon`` executable to simulate a 32-bit Hexagon "
"machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:12
msgid "Hexagon Machines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:14
msgid ""
"Hexagon DSPs are suited to various functions and generally appear in a \"DSP "
"subsystem\" of a larger system-on-chip (SoC)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:17
msgid ""
"Hexagon DSPs are often included in a subsystem that looks like the diagram "
"below.  Instructions are loaded into DDR before the DSP is brought out of "
"reset and the first instructions are fetched from DDR via the EVB/reset "
"vector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:21
msgid ""
"In a real system, a TBU/SMMU would normally arbitrate AXI accesses but we "
"don't have a need to model that for QEMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:24
msgid ""
"Hexagon DSP cores use simultaneous multithreading (SMT) with as many as 8 "
"hardware threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:27
msgid "Diagram"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:29
msgid ""
"       AHB (local) bus                     AXI (global) bus\n"
"             │                                 │\n"
"             │                                 │\n"
"┌─────────┐  │       ┌─────────────────┐       │\n"
"│ L2VIC   ├──┤       │                 │       │\n"
"│         ├──┼───────►                 ├───────┤\n"
"└─────▲───┘  │       │   Hexagon DSP   │       │\n"
"      │      │       │                 │       │        ┌─────┐\n"
"      │      │       │    N threads    │       │        │ DDR │\n"
"      │      ├───────┤                 │       │        │     │\n"
" ┌────┴──┐   │       │                 │       ├────────┤     │\n"
" │QTimer ├───┤       │                 │       │        │     │\n"
" │       │   │       │                 │       │        │     │\n"
" └───────┘   │       │   ┌─────────┐   │       │        │     │\n"
"             │       │  ┌─────────┐│   │       │        │     │\n"
" ┌───────┐   │       │  │  HVX xM ││   │       │        │     │\n"
" │QDSP6SS├───┤       │  │         │┘   │       │        │     │\n"
" └───────┘   │       │  └─────────┘    │       │        └─────┘\n"
"             │       │                 │       │\n"
" ┌───────┐   │       └─────────────────┘       │\n"
" │  CSR  ├───┤\n"
" └───────┘   │   ┌──────┐   ┌───────────┐\n"
"             │   │ TCM  │   │   VTCM    │\n"
"                 │      │   │           │\n"
"                 └──────┘   │           │\n"
"                            │           │\n"
"                            │           │\n"
"                            │           │\n"
"                            └───────────┘"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:62
msgid "Components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:63
msgid ""
"Other than l2vic and HVX, the components below are not implemented in QEMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:65
msgid ""
"L2VIC: the L2 vectored interrupt controller.  Supports 1024 input "
"interrupts, edge- or level-triggered.  The core ISA has system registers "
"``VID``, ``VID1`` which read through to the L2VIC device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:68
msgid ""
"QTimer: ARMSSE-based programmable timer device. Its interrupts are wired to "
"the L2VIC.  System registers ``TIMER``, ``UTIMER`` read through to the "
"QTimer device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:71
msgid ""
"QDSP6SS: DSP subsystem features, accessible to the entire SoC, including DSP "
"NMI, watchdog, reset, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:73
msgid "CSR: Configuration/Status Registers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:74
msgid ""
"TCM: DSP-exclusive tightly-coupled memory.  This memory can be used for DSPs "
"when isolated from DDR and in some bootstrapping modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:76
msgid ""
"VTCM: DSP-exclusive vector tightly-coupled memory.  This memory is accessed "
"by some HVX instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:78
msgid ""
"HVX: the vector coprocessor supports 64 and 128-byte vector registers. 64-"
"byte mode is not implemented in QEMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:83
msgid "Bootstrapping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:84
msgid ""
"Hexagon systems do not generally have access to a block device.  So, for "
"QEMU the typical use case involves loading a binary or ELF file into memory "
"and executing from the indicated start address::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:88
msgid "$ qemu-system-hexagon -kernel ./prog -append 'arg1 arg2'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:91
msgid "Semihosting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/target-hexagon.rst:92
msgid ""
"Hexagon supports a semihosting interface similar to other architectures'. "
"The ``trap0`` instruction can activate these semihosting calls so that the "
"guest software can access the host console and filesystem.  Semihosting is "
"not yet implemented in QEMU hexagon."
msgstr ""

